    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. The only test class in the repo is `AcceptanceTest` (2 tests), and both are green with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the derived `ownerSegment` field on the owner read model.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`mapper/OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 a standalone helper mirroring the existing `AgeBand`/`OwnerLocality` pattern. `OwnerSegment.of(membershipLevel, locality)` returns `'<TIER>_<AREA>'`:\n   - TIER = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3`, else `STANDARD` (null level \u2192 STANDARD).\n   - AREA = `METRO` when locality \u2208 {NSW, VIC, QLD}, else `REGIONAL`.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 registered `OwnerSegment` in the mapper's `imports` and added a `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` that feeds it `owner.getMembershipLevel()` and the locality resolved via the existing `OwnerLocality.fromCustomerCode(owner.getCustomerCode())` (the same source the `locality`/`timezone` fields already use, so the segment shares the region identity assigned at creation).\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time), documenting the four possible values.\n\nThe acceptance tests confirm both cases: a Sydney (NSW) owner at membership level 2 \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`, and an unknown-city owner \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`.",
